ree metres, with Rudolph winning her third gold medal. Rudolph had received the baton from " [:a {:href "/athletes/77881"} "Pearl Jones"] ", who had also won a gold medal in the 1952 4x100 relay, when she was only 15 years old. Germany’s third leg was run by " [:a {:href "/athletes/70003"} "Brunhilde Hendrix"] " whose mother, " [:a {:href "/athletes/69968"} "Marie Dollinger"] ", had run the third leg for Germany in 1936, when she had " [:a {:href "/athletes/69970"} "Ilse Dörffeldt"] " botched the exchange, Dörffeldt dropping the baton. Hendrix’s father had also run in an Olympic relay, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/70274"} "Fritz Hendrix"] " running for Germany in 1932 in the 4x1."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "44.4 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "44.5 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/77867"} "Martha Hudson"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/78013"} "Lucinda Williams"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77881"} "Barbara Jones"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77958"} "Wilma Rudolph"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77938"} "Ernestine Pollards"] [:small {} " (DNS)"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/78009"} "Willye White"] [:small {} " (DNS)"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Unified Team of Germany"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "45.8 (2 h1)"] [:td